   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-27",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The opposition supported the Competition and Consumer Amendment Bill 2013, which exempts restaurants and cafes from requiring separate menus for surcharge days, implementing a Productivity Commission recommendation and reducing compliance costs estimated at $8,000–$10,000 per business. The coalition also announced a future root-and-branch review of competition law, including unfair contract provisions for small businesses."
  }
